      "writtenOn": "2025-10-16T17:49:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, I\u0027ve just noticed that pgtable_unmap_cb() never gets a non-NULL data-\u003ememcache anyway (a memcache is passed to pkvm_pgtable_map() only, not to pkvm_pgtable_unmap()). And yeah, it makes sense.\n\nStill, related note: it still seems it would be good to check if the memcache is NULL in guest_mmu_zalloc_page() (to let it return NULL and let its caller return -ENOMEM, instead of crashing the hypervisor)?",
